\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For a connected-fiber surjective morphism $f:X\to Y$ of smooth connected projective complex varieties with smooth geometric generic fiber F of $\kappa (F)=0$, suppose $m_{0}K_X-f*H$ is pseudo-effective for some $m_{0}>0$ and ample Cartier H on Y. Must $\kappa (X)=dim$ Y?

\subsection{Short English statement}
For a connected-fiber surjective morphism $f:X\to Y$ of smooth connected projective complex varieties with smooth geometric generic fiber F of $\kappa (F)=0$, suppose $m_{0}K_X-f*H$ is pseudo-effective for some $m_{0}>0$ and ample Cartier H on Y. Must $\kappa (X)=dim$ Y?

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] Original question source or mathematical context.
\url{https://arxiv.org/abs/0806.4413}.
\item[S2] OpenAI, manuscript citation page. Source of the formulation motivating this local problem.
\url{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/Schnell-fiber-spaces-and-good-canonical-models-September-24-2026/README.md}.
\end{itemize}

