\section*{Schnell’s fiber-space assertion in Kodaira dimension zero}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
The Campana--Peternell Kodaira inequality and the specified Schnell fiber-space conclusion are claimed from a pseudo-effective difference between a canonical multiple and the chosen effective or pulled-back divisor. The cited manuscript argues for that result; its relation to this problem is specified below.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
Manuscript 1 (family 034, 2026-09-24): The total-space canonical model, with its good-model property, supplies the geometric reduction. Cartier intersection theory and proper pushforward compare the base with the canonical image without requiring either map to factor through the other; transfer of sections then yields the Kodaira and fiber formulas.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
